SCIENTIFIC SCOPE
- Candidate distributions are compared rather than imposed.
- Lognormal and Weibull from the approved research design are evaluated alongside Gamma and Exponential.
- All models use maximum-likelihood estimation with loc=0.
- AIC/AICc/BIC compare relative model support; they do not prove that a distribution is true.
- Nominal KS/CvM p-values are retained only as diagnostics because parameters are estimated from the same observations.
- Parametric-bootstrap KS calibration is therefore reported.
- Quantile diagnostics evaluate practical reproduction of the observed award-time distribution.
- Bootstrap model-selection frequencies evaluate stability under resampling.
- P25/P75 fitting is retained as scenario-definition robustness.
- Data-driven scenarios are not used for primary fitting because the High group has only n=8.
- No observations are deleted.
- No Monte Carlo award-time simulation is performed.
- No discrete-event simulation is performed.
- No causal interpretation is imposed.

